<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Unified Framework</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we establish a theoretical framework that unifies guidance methods under the perspective of fixed-point iterations. Through systematic examination of Classifier-Free Guidance (CFG), its variant CFG++, and reflective sampling techniques including Z-Sampling and Resampling, we demonstrate how these approaches achieve conditional generation through distinct yet analogous fixed point operators. Our framework decouples guidance to denoising-agnostic calibration steps, facilitating the design of guidance algorithms.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Classifier-Free Guidance (CFG) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Classifier-Free Guidance (CFG) enhances conditional generation by interpolating conditional and unconditional noise predictions during the diffusion process. Our analysis reveals that CFG’s forward process corresponds to a linear fixed-point operator with consistency intervals spanning <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to t-1</annotation></semantics></math>, requiring 1 NFE per iteration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To formalize this, we begin with the DDIM update step governed by the predicted noise <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t-1}=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\left[x_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon(x_{t})\right]+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\epsilon(x_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t-1}=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\left[x_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon(x_{t})\right]+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\epsilon(x_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}_{t}=\prod_{i=1}^{t}\alpha_{i}=\alpha_{t}\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\alpha}_{t}=\prod_{i=1}^{t}\alpha_{i}=\alpha_{t}\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Through algebraic rearrangement, we derive an equivalent representation that better elucidates the noise dependency:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}x_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)\epsilon(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}x_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)\epsilon(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}x_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)\epsilon(x_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}x_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)\epsilon(x_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">CFG introduces a rescaled noise prediction to amplify conditional guidance:</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{w}(x_{t})=\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})+w(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{w}(x_{t})=\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})+w(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> modulates guidance strength. Substituting <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{w}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{w}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> into the update rule yields:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}x_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}x_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\times\left[\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})+w(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\times\left[\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})+w(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This formulation admits an insightful reinterpretation as a two-step process. First, the latent variable <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is calibrated via:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{t}=x_{t}-w\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{t}=x_{t}-w\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">followed by an unconditional denoise:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t-1}=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\hat{x}_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t-1}=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\hat{x}_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The iterative variant CFG<math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times K</annotation></semantics></math> is detailed in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ A.2 CFG++ [] ‣ Appendix A Unified Framework ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>CFG++  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CFG++ derives conditional guidance through manifold constraints formulated from an inverse problem perspective, closely aligned with CFG in implementation. Our analysis demonstrates that CFG++ similarly corresponds to a linear fixed-point operator iteration but diverges from CFG solely in its strength scheduling strategy, retaining the consistency interval <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to t-1</annotation></semantics></math> at a computational cost of 1 NFE per iteration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">CFG++ adjust the guidance strength through parameter <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> applied to the noise difference term:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\left\{x_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}[\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})+\lambda(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))]\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\left\{x_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}[\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})+\lambda(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))]\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This admits similar calibration-interpretation, where the latent calibration becomes:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{t}=x_{t}-\lambda\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{t}=x_{t}-\lambda\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">followed by the same unconditional update:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t-1}=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\hat{x}_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t-1}=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\hat{x}_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Both CFG and CFG++ exhibit fixed-point behavior through linear operators:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{\text{CFG}}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>CFG</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{\text{CFG}}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{t}+w\xi_{t}(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{t}+w\xi_{t}(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{\text{CFG++}}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>CFG++</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{\text{CFG++}}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{t}+\lambda\tilde{\xi}_{t}(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{t}+\lambda\tilde{\xi}_{t}(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}=\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right),\tilde{\xi}_{t}=\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}=\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right),\tilde{\xi}_{t}=\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Note that fixed-point <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x_{t})=x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x_{t})=x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> implies consistency <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})=\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})=\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, enforcing alignment between conditional and unconditional update paths: <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{t\to t-1}(x_{t})=f^{c}_{t\to t-1}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{t\to t-1}(x_{t})=f^{c}_{t\to t-1}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. The iterative variant CFG++<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times K</annotation></semantics></math> is detailed in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ A.2 CFG++ [] ‣ Appendix A Unified Framework ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
