</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Z-Sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Z-sampling augments conditional guidance by reflective sampling steps: inversion using unconditional noise followed by forward using high-strength guided noise. This procedure is mathematically equivalent to a fixed-point iteration using an backward-forward operator. When integrated with CFG after reflective sampling updates, the process achieves a consistency interval of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1\to t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1\to t-1</annotation></semantics></math> at a cost of 3 NFE per iteration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Z-Sampling enforces backward-forward consistency via the relation:</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=f^{\gamma}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})\implies x_{t}=f^{\gamma^{-1}}_{t\to t+1}\circ f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=f^{\gamma}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})\implies x_{t}=f^{\gamma^{-1}}_{t\to t+1}\circ f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes denoising with noise <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{u}+\gamma(\epsilon^{c}-\epsilon^{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{u}+\gamma(\epsilon^{c}-\epsilon^{u})</annotation></semantics></math>. In fact, the equality <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=f^{\gamma}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=f^{\gamma}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as a generalization of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=f^{c}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=f^{c}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. This stems from the relationship: <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})=\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})=\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})=\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})+\gamma[\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})=\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})+\gamma[\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math>, which establishes that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=f^{c}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=f^{c}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> can be extended to <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=f^{\gamma}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=f^{\gamma}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Approximating the inverse process <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\gamma^{-1}}_{t\to t+1}\approx f^{\gamma}_{t+1\to t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msubsup><mo>≈</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\gamma^{-1}}_{t\to t+1}\approx f^{\gamma}_{t+1\to t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we derive:</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}_{t}=f^{c}_{t+1\to t}\circ f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}_{t}=f^{c}_{t+1\to t}\circ f^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Subsequent application of CFG’s calibration step yields:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{x}_{t}-w\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)(\epsilon^{c}(\tilde{x}_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(\tilde{x}_{t}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{x}_{t}-w\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)(\epsilon^{c}(\tilde{x}_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(\tilde{x}_{t})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\hat{x}_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)\epsilon^{u}(\tilde{x}_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\hat{x}_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)\epsilon^{u}(\tilde{x}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This constructs a composite fixed-point iteration over the extended interval <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1\to t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1\to t-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Resampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite></h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Resampling also utilizes backward-forward fixed-point iterations but differs by incorporating a model-free stochastic noise function for the inversion step. Consequently, it maintains the <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1\to t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1\to t-1</annotation></semantics></math> update interval while reducing the computational cost to 2 NFE per iteration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The stochastic backward step is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}x_{t}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\epsilon,\quad\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})=\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}x_{t}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\epsilon,\quad\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which leads to the complete update sequence:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f^{\gamma}_{t+1\to t}\circ n^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f^{\gamma}_{t+1\to t}\circ n^{u}_{t\to t+1}(x_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{x}_{t}-w\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)(\epsilon^{c}(\tilde{x}_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(\tilde{x}_{t}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{x}_{t}-w\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)(\epsilon^{c}(\tilde{x}_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(\tilde{x}_{t})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\hat{x}_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)\epsilon^{u}(\tilde{x}_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\hat{x}_{t}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\right)\epsilon^{u}(\tilde{x}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Although computationally efficient, the stochastic approximation <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{t\to t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{t\to t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> introduces semantic distortion compared to deterministic counterparts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We demonstrate that Resampling can be viewed as an approximation of Z-Sampling when the step size is sufficiently small and <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large. First, we express the DDIM forward process <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\gamma}_{t+1\to t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\gamma}_{t+1\to t}</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly:</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\gamma}_{t+1\to t}(x_{t+1})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}}x_{t+1}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}}\right)\epsilon^{\gamma}(x_{t+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\gamma}_{t+1\to t}(x_{t+1})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}}x_{t+1}+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}}\right)\epsilon^{\gamma}(x_{t+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">For a sufficiently small step size, we approximate <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon(x_{t+1})\approx\epsilon(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon(x_{t+1})\approx\epsilon(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and substitute <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}=\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}x_{t}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}=\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}x_{t}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the fixed-point update form:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E29X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}}(\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}x_{t}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\epsilon)+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}}\right)\epsilon^{\gamma}(x_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}}(\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}x_{t}+\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t+1}}\epsilon)+\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\frac{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}}\right)\epsilon^{\gamma}(x_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E29Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{t}+m_{t}\epsilon+n_{t}[\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})+\gamma(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{t}+m_{t}\epsilon+n_{t}[\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})+\gamma(\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t}))],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}=\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t+1}}/\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}=\sqrt{1-\alpha_{t+1}}/\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{t}=\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}/\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{t}=\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}/\sqrt{\alpha_{t+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> are time-dependent constants. Compared to the fixed-point objective <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})=0</annotation></semantics></math> of other operators, the objective for Resampling’s fixed-point operator becomes:</p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})=\frac{1}{\gamma}[m_{t}\epsilon-n_{t}\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{c}(x_{t})-\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})=\frac{1}{\gamma}[m_{t}\epsilon-n_{t}\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Theoretically, the objective of Resampling aligns with other fixed-point operators when <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large. In practice, however, <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is not set to an extremely large value to maintain sample quality, which causes Resampling to underperform compared to other operators. Nevertheless, Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3.2 Foresight Guidance ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows that Resampling still benefits from increased iteration counts. This empirically confirms that Resampling’s fixed-point operator is a functional, albeit suboptimal, choice.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This systematic analysis demonstrates how various guidance methods can be unified under our fixed point framework, as summarized in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.1 Towards the Golden Path via Fixed Point Iterations ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> of the main text.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Comparison of Design Choices</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides a comprehensive analysis of the design choices within our unified fixed point iteration framework, examining both iteration strength schedulers and fixed point operators.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Iteration strength schedulers.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The schedulers for CFG and CFG++ are given by <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}=\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}=\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\xi}_{t}=\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\xi}_{t}=\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Using the <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> setting in DDIM as an example, Figure <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Iteration strength schedulers. ‣ A.5 Comparison of Design Choices ‣ Appendix A Unified Framework ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\xi}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\xi}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at different timesteps.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:39%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.21512v1/Scheduler_comparison.svg" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:181/169;" width="181" height="169"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Comparison of iteration strength schedulers for CFG (<math id="A1.F6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) and CFG++ (<math id="A1.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\xi}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\xi}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) across different timesteps.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It can be observed that, in the early stages where guidance has a greater impact on generation (<math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0.67,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.67</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0.67,1]</annotation></semantics></math>), the guidance strength provided by <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> decays rapidly, which limits generation quality. In contrast, <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\xi}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\xi}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> provides more stable iteration strength during these critical early stages, explaining the improved stability of CFG++ over CFG. The mathematical derivation of these schedulers reveals that <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> contains an additional term <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> that causes the rapid decay, while <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\xi}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\xi}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> maintains a more gradual decrease throughout the diffusion process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Fixed point operators.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In FSG, a forward-backward operator with a larger interval <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> is selected, as it exhibits a smaller contraction rate, thereby accelerating the convergence of the fixed-point algorithm.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Due to the complexity of neural networks, a direct computation of the model’s contraction rate is infeasible. Instead, we employ an empirical estimation of the local contraction rate within a neighborhood of <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as a set of points generated by mixing the same <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with slightly different noises. The local contraction rate for an operator <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> under the <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm is measured as:</p>
<table id="A1.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p(x)}\frac{\lVert F(x_{t})-F(x_{t}^{\prime})\rVert_{2}^{2}}{\lVert x_{t}-x_{t}^{\prime}\rVert_{2}^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p(x)}\frac{\lVert F(x_{t})-F(x_{t}^{\prime})\rVert_{2}^{2}}{\lVert x_{t}-x_{t}^{\prime}\rVert_{2}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t},x_{t}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t},x_{t}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are obtained by mixing different noises with <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>Empirical contraction rates <math id="A1.T9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}</annotation></semantics></math> for different operators across denoising timesteps.</figcaption>
<table id="A1.T9.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T9.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">Operators</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;"><math id="A1.T9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=</annotation></semantics></math>0.2</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;"><math id="A1.T9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=</annotation></semantics></math>0.4</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;"><math id="A1.T9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=</annotation></semantics></math>0.6</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;"><math id="A1.T9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=</annotation></semantics></math>0.8</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;"><math id="A1.T9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{id}-w_{t}\Delta\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>id</mtext><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{id}-w_{t}\Delta\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (CFG, CFG++)</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">1.00</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">1.00</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">1.00</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">1.00</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;"><math id="A1.T9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\gamma}_{t+dt\to t}\circ f^{u}_{t\to t+dt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\gamma}_{t+dt\to t}\circ f^{u}_{t\to t+dt}</annotation></semantics></math> (Z-sampling)</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">1.04</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.99</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.97</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.99</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;"><math id="A1.T9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\gamma}_{t+dt\to t}\circ n^{u}_{t\to t+dt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\gamma}_{t+dt\to t}\circ n^{u}_{t\to t+dt}</annotation></semantics></math> (Resampling)</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.89</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.97</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">1.03</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">1.07</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;"><math id="A1.T9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{t/2\to t}\circ f^{\gamma}_{t\to t/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{t/2\to t}\circ f^{\gamma}_{t\to t/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">1.03</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.95</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.96</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.98</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;"><math id="A1.T9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{t/4\to t}\circ f^{\gamma}_{t\to t/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{t/4\to t}\circ f^{\gamma}_{t\to t/4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.61</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.91</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.88</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.91</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;"><math id="A1.T9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{0\to t}\circ f^{\gamma}_{t\to 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{0\to t}\circ f^{\gamma}_{t\to 0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.62</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.70</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.75</td>
<td id="A1.T9.2.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.79</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Notably, long-interval operators (e.g., <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{0\to t}\circ f^{\gamma}_{t\to 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{0\to t}\circ f^{\gamma}_{t\to 0}</annotation></semantics></math>) demonstrate lower contraction rates (<math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{r}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{r}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>) compared to short-interval operators such as Z-sampling or Resampling. To balance convergence speed and operator complexity, we select an intermediate interval <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dt&lt;\Delta t&lt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dt&lt;\Delta t&lt;t</annotation></semantics></math>) for the operator <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}_{t-\Delta t\to t}\circ f^{\gamma}_{t\to t-\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}_{t-\Delta t\to t}\circ f^{\gamma}_{t\to t-\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The contraction rate of an operator depends on the choice of metric. While operators in CFG/CFG++ are non-contracting under the <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm, they may exhibit contraction in other carefully designed metrics. Empirically, as shown in Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 3.2 Foresight Guidance ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, these methods also benefit from additional iterations, supporting the fixed-point framework.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Discussion of Golden Path</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The concept of the golden path, wherein latent representations yield consistent outputs under both conditional and unconditional generation, is central to our framework. This section provides empirical evidence supporting this theoretical foundation and demonstrates its practical implications. We construct matched and unmatched samples <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (on and off the golden path, respectively) by design.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Match case:</span> An image <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated conditioned on a prompt <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. We then obtain <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> via DDIM inversion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> using unconditional noise <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{u}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}=f_{0\to t}^{u}(x^{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}=f_{0\to t}^{u}(x^{c})</annotation></semantics></math>. These <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> exhibit consistency between conditional and unconditional generation paths, satisfying <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{c}\approx f^{u}_{t\to 0}(x_{t})\approx f^{c}_{t\to 0}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{c}\approx f^{u}_{t\to 0}(x_{t})\approx f^{c}_{t\to 0}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mismatch case:</span> For each matched sample, we assign a different prompt <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}\neq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}\neq c</annotation></semantics></math> to create a mismatch, where <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{c}\approx f^{u}_{t\to 0}(x_{t})\neq f^{c^{\prime}}_{t\to 0}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{c}\approx f^{u}_{t\to 0}(x_{t})\neq f^{c^{\prime}}_{t\to 0}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T10" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:50%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Performance from <math id="A2.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> under matched (<math id="A2.T10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>) and mismatched (<math id="A2.T10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}\neq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}\neq c</annotation></semantics></math>) conditions.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T10.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A2.T10.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T10.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="A2.T10.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="A2.T10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;" colspan="2">IR</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;" colspan="2">HPSv2</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T10.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T10.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">Match</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">Mismatch</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">Match</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">Mismatch</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T10.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T10.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.8</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">97.09</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">-69.96</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">28.85</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">25.02</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T10.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T10.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.6</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">89.45</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">-171.16</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">28.73</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">22.84</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T10.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T10.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.4</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">84.42</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">-196.38</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">28.53</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">21.86</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T10.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T10.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">0.2</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">81.43</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">-201.60</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">28.47</td>
<td id="A2.T10.2.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:1pt 3.0pt;">21.53</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using these <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as starting points, we evaluate generation performance under matched and mismatched prompt conditions using CFG <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>. As shown in Table <a href="#A2.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix B Discussion of Golden Path ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, when <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{c/u}{t\to 0}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{c/u}{t\to 0}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is mismatched, both the alignment and quality of the generated images decrease significantly. Intuitively, when <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{u}{t\to 0}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{u}{t\to 0}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> aligns poorly with condition <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, a larger proportion of the components in <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> become unsuitable for generating content consistent with <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. This forces the diffusion model to make more substantial corrections within the limited <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> interval, ultimately compromising generation quality and prompt adherence. These results empirically validate our theoretical framework and motivate the use of fixed-point iterations to achieve golden path consistency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now present the theoretical foundations for FSG, summarized in <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.2 Foresight Guidance ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. We first clarify the notations and state the key assumptions. Under mild conditions, we provide theoretical guidance for allocating the total number of fixed-point iterations <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall that we partition the diffusion process into <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> intervals <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\to t_{i}-\Delta t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\to t_{i}-\Delta t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,M</annotation></semantics></math>, and perform <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed-point iterations on each interval using a forward-backward operator <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}:=F_{t_{i}\to t_{i}-\Delta t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}:=F_{t_{i}\to t_{i}-\Delta t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, for each iteration <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for FSG:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Starting from <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t_{i}}^{(j-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{i}}^{(j-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, apply the conditionally-guided ODE solver <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\gamma}_{t_{i}\to t_{i}-\Delta t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\gamma}_{t_{i}\to t_{i}-\Delta t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t_{i}-\Delta t_{i}}^{(j-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{i}-\Delta t_{i}}^{(j-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Then, use the unconditionally-guided reverse ODE solver <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\gamma}_{t_{i}-\Delta t_{i}\to t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\gamma}_{t_{i}-\Delta t_{i}\to t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> to map back and update <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t_{i}}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{i}}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This forward-backward procedure iteratively calibrates <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> by leveraging both conditional and unconditional guidance over the interval, promoting consistency between the two trajectories. For other methods such as CFG and CFG++, the operator <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be defined as described in <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Unified Framework ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> (Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Unified Framework ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>). Our analysis remains applicable under these definitions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For the clarity of theoretical analysis, we consider a fixed-length interval partition, setting each interval to size <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> so that the total number of timesteps <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is divided into <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=T/W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=T/W</annotation></semantics></math> intervals. We assume <math id="A3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> divides <math id="A3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, and allocate <math id="A3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=N/M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=N/M</annotation></semantics></math> fixed-point iterations to calibrate each <math id="A3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}=iW" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}=iW</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,M</annotation></semantics></math>.
This leads to the following procedure to produce the trajectory <math id="A3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from given <math id="A3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{t}=\begin{cases}F_{t\rightarrow t-W}^{K}\left(x_{t}\right),&amp;\text{if }t\bmod W=0\\
x_{t},&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases},\quad x_{t-1}=f_{t\rightarrow t-1}^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t}\right),\quad t=1\dots T." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{t}=\begin{cases}F_{t\rightarrow t-W}^{K}\left(x_{t}\right),&amp;\text{if }t\bmod W=0\\
x_{t},&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases},\quad x_{t-1}=f_{t\rightarrow t-1}^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t}\right),\quad t=1\dots T.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{u}\left(x,t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{u}\left(x,t\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{c}\left(x,t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{c}\left(x,t\right)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the unconditional and conditional noise predictions, respectively.
The domain regarding <math id="A3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> for all the functions, including <math id="A3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x,t\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x,t\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{a\rightarrow b}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{a\rightarrow b}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, etc., is assumed to be <math id="A3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (unless otherwise specified). And we use <math id="A3.p5.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the Euclidean norm in <math id="A3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Key assumptions are as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Boundedness:</span>
The latent variables and noise predictions are bounded, i.e., <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{x}_{t}\|,\|\epsilon^{c/u}(\hat{x}_{t})\|\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{x}_{t}\|,\|\epsilon^{c/u}(\hat{x}_{t})\|\leq B</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#Thmass1" title="Assumption 1 (Boundedness). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Smoothness:</span>
The noise functions <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{c/u}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{c/u}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> are Lipschitz continuous with a smoothness constant <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#Thmass2" title="Assumption 2 (Smoothness of Noise). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). Additionally, the ODE dynamics derived from these noise functions are smooth (<a href="#Thmass3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contraction:</span>
The fixed-point operator <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction with a rate bounded by <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#Thmass4" title="Assumption 4 (Contraction and Fixed Point Existence). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Building on the assumptions, we establish a framework for optimizing the allocation of fixed-point iterations. For the procedure described in <a href="#A3.E32" title="In Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">​​</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>, we analyze the allocation of iterations across intervals <math id="A3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[(i-1)W,iW]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[(i-1)W,iW]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[1,M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[1,M]</annotation></semantics></math>, where the fixed-point operator <math id="A3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{iW\rightarrow(i-1)W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{iW\rightarrow(i-1)W}</annotation></semantics></math> is applied. The sampling ratio is defined as:</p>
<table id="A3.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta:=\frac{1}{M}=\frac{K}{N}=\frac{W}{T}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta:=\frac{1}{M}=\frac{K}{N}=\frac{W}{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of intervals, <math id="A3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of iterations per interval, <math id="A3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of iterations, and <math id="A3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of timesteps. We derive an upper bound to guide the optimal choice of <math id="A3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheoremx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheoremx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem</span></span><span id="Thmtheoremx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(detailed version of <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.2 Foresight Guidance ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)<span id="Thmtheoremx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheoremx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that <a href="#Thmass1" title="Assumption 1 (Boundedness). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumptions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <a href="#Thmass3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <a href="#Thmass2" title="Assumption 2 (Smoothness of Noise). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmass4" title="Assumption 4 (Contraction and Fixed Point Existence). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> hold. Let <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the trajectory produced as in <a href="#A3.E32" title="In Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">​​</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>, with <math id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\frac{1}{M}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\frac{1}{M}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists an upper bound function:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\beta,L,r)=\left(\Theta(1)+\Theta(L^{2})\right)r^{2\beta N}+2L^{2}\beta^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\beta,L,r)=\left(\Theta(1)+\Theta(L^{2})\right)r^{2\beta N}+2L^{2}\beta^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheoremx1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">such that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\right\|^{2}\leq B^{2}Tg(\beta,L,r)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\right\|^{2}\leq B^{2}Tg(\beta,L,r).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is deferred to the end of this section.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(f(L))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(f(L))</annotation></semantics></math> denotes an upper bound up to a constant, i.e., <math id="A3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq Cf(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq Cf(L)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(f(L))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(f(L))</annotation></semantics></math> denotes both upper and lower bounds up to constants, i.e., <math id="A3.p10.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="cf(L)\leq\cdot\leq Cf(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cf(L)\leq\cdot\leq Cf(L)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <a href="#Thmass1" title="Assumption 1 (Boundedness). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> provides a trivial bound <math id="A3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\leq 4B^{2}T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\leq 4B^{2}T</annotation></semantics></math>, while large <math id="A3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> may lead to <math id="A3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\beta,L,r)&gt;4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\beta,L,r)&gt;4</annotation></semantics></math>, so our bound is more meaningful for smooth noise function with smaller <math id="A3.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A3.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the bound simplifies to:</p>
<table id="A3.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\beta,L,r)=\Theta(r^{2\beta N})+2L^{2}\beta^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\beta,L,r)=\Theta(r^{2\beta N})+2L^{2}\beta^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimal <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> for minimizing <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\beta,L,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\beta,L,r)</annotation></semantics></math>:</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For fixed <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by solving:</p>
<table id="A3.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\beta}g(\beta,L,r)=4L^{2}\beta-\Theta\left(2N\ln(1/r)(1/r)^{-2\beta N}\right)=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\beta}g(\beta,L,r)=4L^{2}\beta-\Theta\left(2N\ln(1/r)(1/r)^{-2\beta N}\right)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}\beta=\Theta(N\ln(1/r)(1/r)^{-2\beta N})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}\beta=\Theta(N\ln(1/r)(1/r)^{-2\beta N}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}\beta</annotation></semantics></math> increases linearly with <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, while the term <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\ln(1/r)(1/r)^{-2\beta N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\ln(1/r)(1/r)^{-2\beta N}</annotation></semantics></math> decays exponentially, guaranteeing a unique minimizer <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Importantly, as the noise smoothness <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> decreases, the optimal <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> increases, suggesting that smoother noise allows for fewer, longer intervals (i.e., larger <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>). Conversely, as the total iteration budget <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> grows, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> approaches zero, recovering the short-interval setting (<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=T</annotation></semantics></math>) as a limiting case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we formalize the boundedness assumptions for images and noise, which are standard in diffusion model analysis:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmass1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_ass">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmass1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmass1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Boundedness)<span id="Thmass1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmass1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmass1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmass1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists <math id="Thmass1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmass1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="Thmass1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{M}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{M}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|\leq B,\quad\|\varepsilon^{u}\left(x,t\right)\|\leq B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|\leq B,\quad\|\varepsilon^{u}\left(x,t\right)\|\leq B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For images with entries in <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and size <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}\times d_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}\times d_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we may take <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=d_{1}d_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=d_{1}d_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\sqrt{d_{1}d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\sqrt{d_{1}d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We next formalize the smoothness properties of the noise function, introducing a constant <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> that is independent of the data dimension <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of diffusion steps <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmass2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_ass">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmass2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmass2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smoothness of Noise)<span id="Thmass2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmass2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmass2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmass2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a smoothness constant <math id="Thmass2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in(0,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in(0,C)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that the following properties hold for any initial point <math id="Thmass2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and time interval <math id="Thmass2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmass2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Smoothness at a fixed time:</span><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For any </span><math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and any pair of points </span><math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the noise function satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{1},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{2},t\right)\|\leq L\|x_{1}-x_{2}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{1},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{2},t\right)\|\leq L\|x_{1}-x_{2}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Smoothness over varying time:</span><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let </span><math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{u/c}=f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{u/c}=f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for </span><math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then, for any </span><math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1},t_{2}\in[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1},t_{2}\in[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the noise function satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{t_{1}}^{u},t_{1}\right)-\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{t_{2}}^{u},t_{2}\right)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{t_{1}}^{u},t_{1}\right)-\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{t_{2}}^{u},t_{2}\right)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq LB\frac{|t_{1}-t_{2}|}{T}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq LB\frac{|t_{1}-t_{2}|}{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{t_{1}}^{c},t_{1}\right)-\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{t_{2}}^{c},t_{2}\right)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{t_{1}}^{c},t_{1}\right)-\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{t_{2}}^{c},t_{2}\right)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq LB\frac{|t_{1}-t_{2}|}{T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq LB\frac{|t_{1}-t_{2}|}{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Building on the smoothness of noise (<a href="#Thmass2" title="Assumption 2 (Smoothness of Noise). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), we analyze the properties of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math> represents an ODE evolving from time <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, initialized at point <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. The ODE is defined as:</p>
<table id="A3.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}\left(\frac{x_{t}^{u/c}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\right)=\frac{d}{dt}\left(\sqrt{\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\right)\varepsilon_{\theta}^{u/c}\left(x_{t}^{u/c},t\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}\left(\frac{x_{t}^{u/c}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\right)=\frac{d}{dt}\left(\sqrt{\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\right)\varepsilon_{\theta}^{u/c}\left(x_{t}^{u/c},t\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the parameters of the neural network, which we omit for simplicity in subsequent discussions. This ODE yields the following explicit form for the time derivative of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{u/c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{u/c}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dx_{t}^{u/c}}{dt}=\mu_{t}x_{t}^{u/c}+\lambda_{t}\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{t}^{u/c},t\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dx_{t}^{u/c}}{dt}=\mu_{t}x_{t}^{u/c}+\lambda_{t}\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x_{t}^{u/c},t\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A3.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t_{0}}:=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\,\frac{d}{dt}\left(\sqrt{\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\right)\Big|_{t=t_{0}},\quad\mu_{t_{0}}:=-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\,\frac{d}{dt}\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\right)\Big|_{t=t_{0}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t_{0}}:=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\,\frac{d}{dt}\left(\sqrt{\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\right)\Big|_{t=t_{0}},\quad\mu_{t_{0}}:=-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\,\frac{d}{dt}\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\right)\Big|_{t=t_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmass3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_ass">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmass3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span></span><span id="Thmass3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmass3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmass3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmass3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmass3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> be the smoothness constant in <a href="#Thmass2" title="Assumption 2 (Smoothness of Noise). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. There exist constants <math id="Thmass3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmass3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmass3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A3.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Smooth Dependence on Initial Error:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(y\right)\|\leq C\ell_{a,b,L}\|x-y\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(y\right)\|\leq C\ell_{a,b,L}\|x-y\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I4.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A3.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,b,L}=(|\lambda_{a}|L+|\mu_{a}|)|b-a|+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,b,L}=(|\lambda_{a}|L+|\mu_{a}|)|b-a|+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Noise Control:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(x\right)\|\geq c\lambda_{a}\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(x,a\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(x,a\right)\||b-a|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(x\right)\|\geq c\lambda_{a}\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(x,a\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(x,a\right)\||b-a|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Motivation:</span>
This assumption is motivated by a first-order Taylor expansion of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x/y\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x/y\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For smoothness on intial error:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.I5.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(y\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(y\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\left.\frac{d}{dt}\left(f_{a\rightarrow t}^{u/c}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow t}^{u/c}\left(y\right)\right)\right|_{t=a}(b-a)+(x-y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\left.\frac{d}{dt}\left(f_{a\rightarrow t}^{u/c}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow t}^{u/c}\left(y\right)\right)\right|_{t=a}(b-a)+(x-y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\mu_{a}(x-y)+\lambda_{a}\left(\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x,a\right)-\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(y,a\right)\right)\right)(b-a)+(x-y)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\mu_{a}(x-y)+\lambda_{a}\left(\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x,a\right)-\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(y,a\right)\right)\right)(b-a)+(x-y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x,a\right)-\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(y,a\right)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(x,a\right)-\varepsilon^{u/c}\left(y,a\right)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L\|x-y\|\mbox{ from \lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{ass:smoothness_of_noise}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext> from </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmass2" title="Assumption 2 (Smoothness of Noise). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L\|x-y\|\mbox{ from \lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{ass:smoothness_of_noise}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(y\right)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u/c}\left(y\right)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\ell_{a,b,L}\|x-y\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\ell_{a,b,L}\|x-y\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.I5.i1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.I5.i1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{a,b,L}:=(|\lambda_{a}|L+|\mu_{a}|)|b-a|+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{a,b,L}:=(|\lambda_{a}|L+|\mu_{a}|)|b-a|+1</annotation></semantics></math> captures the effect of the smoothness of noise, the length of time interval <math id="A3.I5.i1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math> the and dynamics of <math id="A3.I5.i1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\alpha}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> in it. <math id="A3.I5.i1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant that compensates for the error in the Taylor expansion.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For noise control:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(x\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\left.\frac{d}{dt}\left(f_{a\rightarrow t}^{u}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow t}^{c}\left(x\right)\right)\right|_{t=a}(b-a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\left.\frac{d}{dt}\left(f_{a\rightarrow t}^{u}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow t}^{c}\left(x\right)\right)\right|_{t=a}(b-a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{a}\left(\varepsilon^{c}\left(x,a\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(x,a\right)\right)(b-a)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{a}\left(\varepsilon^{c}\left(x,a\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(x,a\right)\right)(b-a),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(y\right)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(x\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(y\right)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq c|\lambda_{a}|\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(x,a\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(x,a\right)\||b-a|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq c|\lambda_{a}|\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(x,a\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(x,a\right)\||b-a|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.I5.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I5.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.I5.i2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> compensates for the error in the Taylor expansion.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Thmass4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_ass">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmass4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 4</span></span><span id="Thmass4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Contraction and Fixed Point Existence)<span id="Thmass4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmass4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmass4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmass4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmass4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. For any time interval <math id="Thmass4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>, the fixed point operator <math id="Thmass4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{a\rightarrow b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{a\rightarrow b}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmass4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A3.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Fixed point equivalence:</span><span id="A3.I6.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
There exists a fixed point </span><math id="A3.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I6.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="A3.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{a\rightarrow b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{a\rightarrow b}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I6.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F_{a\rightarrow b}(x^{*})=x^{*}\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(x^{*}\right)=f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(x^{*}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{a\rightarrow b}(x^{*})=x^{*}\quad\Leftrightarrow\quad f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(x^{*}\right)=f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(x^{*}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Contraction:</span><span id="A3.I6.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For all </span><math id="A3.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I6.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|F_{a\rightarrow b}(x)-F_{a\rightarrow b}(y)\|\leq r\|x-y\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|F_{a\rightarrow b}(x)-F_{a\rightarrow b}(y)\|\leq r\|x-y\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">As an example, the main text considers the fixed point operator <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{a\rightarrow b}(x)=f_{a\to b}^{u_{(-1)}}\circ f_{a\to b}^{c}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{a\rightarrow b}(x)=f_{a\to b}^{u_{(-1)}}\circ f_{a\to b}^{c}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. For brevity, we write <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)</annotation></semantics></math> when the interval <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math> is clear from context.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that <a href="#Thmass1" title="Assumption 1 (Boundedness). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumptions</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <a href="#Thmass3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <a href="#Thmass2" title="Assumption 2 (Smoothness of Noise). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmass4" title="Assumption 4 (Contraction and Fixed Point Existence). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> hold. For any given <math id="Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the following inequality holds:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)\|\leq 2C\ell_{a,b,L}r^{k}\|x-x^{*}\|\leq 4C\ell_{a,b,L}r^{k}B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)\|\leq 2C\ell_{a,b,L}r^{k}\|x-x^{*}\|\leq 4C\ell_{a,b,L}r^{k}B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start by expanding the difference:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-\big(f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)\big)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-\big(f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)\big)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)\|+\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)\|+\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the smoothness property of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(\cdot\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(\cdot\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(\cdot\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(\cdot\right)</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#Thmass3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)\|\leq C\ell_{a,b,L}\|F^{(k)}\left(x\right)-F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)\|\leq C\ell_{a,b,L}\|F^{(k)}\left(x\right)-F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)\|\leq C\ell_{a,b,L}\|F^{(k)}\left(x\right)-F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\right)\|\leq C\ell_{a,b,L}\|F^{(k)}\left(x\right)-F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)\|\leq 2C\ell_{a,b,L}\|F^{(k)}\left(x\right)-F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)\|\leq 2C\ell_{a,b,L}\|F^{(k)}\left(x\right)-F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">Next, applying the contraction property of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#Thmass4" title="Assumption 4 (Contraction and Fixed Point Existence). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|F^{(k)}\left(x\right)-F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\|\leq r^{k}\|x-x^{*}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|F^{(k)}\left(x\right)-F^{(k)}\left(x^{*}\right)\|\leq r^{k}\|x-x^{*}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this into the inequality, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)\|\leq 2\ell_{a,b,L}r^{k}\|x-x^{*}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)\|\leq 2\ell_{a,b,L}r^{k}\|x-x^{*}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.6.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, using the boundedness assumption from <a href="#Thmass1" title="Assumption 1 (Boundedness). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x-x^{*}\|\leq 2B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x-x^{*}\|\leq 2B</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)\|\leq 4\ell_{a,b,L}r^{k}B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{a\rightarrow b}^{c}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)-f_{a\rightarrow b}^{u}\left(F^{(k)}\left(x\right)\right)\|\leq 4\ell_{a,b,L}r^{k}B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.7.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">With these assumptions and lemmas established, we are now ready to prove the main theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We analyze the error in the first interval, as the analysis for other intervals is similar. Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> bes the simplified notation for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{W\rightarrow 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{W\rightarrow 0}</annotation></semantics></math>. The error can be bounded as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E55X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E55X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{W}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E55X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E55Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E55Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)\|^{2}+\sum_{t=1}^{W-1}\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>W</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>W</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)\|^{2}+\sum_{t=1}^{W-1}\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E55Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E55Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(a)}}{{\leq}}(1+3(W-1))\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>W</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>W</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(a)}}{{\leq}}(1+3(W-1))\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E55Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E55Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+3\sum_{t=1}^{W-1}\left(\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)\|^{2}+\|\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)\|^{2}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ε</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ε</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+3\sum_{t=1}^{W-1}\left(\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)\|^{2}+\|\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{W},W\right)\|^{2}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|a+b+c\|^{2}\leq 3(\|a\|^{2}+\|b\|^{2}+\|c\|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|a+b+c\|^{2}\leq 3(\|a\|^{2}+\|b\|^{2}+\|c\|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the bounds in <a href="#Thmass2" title="Assumption 2 (Smoothness of Noise). ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmass3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E56X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E56X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{W}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E56X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E56Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E56Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(3W-2)\|f_{W\rightarrow 0}^{c}\left(F^{(K)}\left(x_{W}\right)\right)-f_{W\rightarrow 0}^{u}\left(F^{(K)}\left(x_{W}\right)\right)\|^{2}\frac{1}{c^{2}\lambda_{W}^{2}W^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(3W-2)\|f_{W\rightarrow 0}^{c}\left(F^{(K)}\left(x_{W}\right)\right)-f_{W\rightarrow 0}^{u}\left(F^{(K)}\left(x_{W}\right)\right)\|^{2}\frac{1}{c^{2}\lambda_{W}^{2}W^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E56Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E56Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+6\frac{B^{2}}{T^{2}}L^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{W-1}(W-i)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mi>L</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+6\frac{B^{2}}{T^{2}}L^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{W-1}(W-i)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E56Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E56Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{lem:fixed_point_error}}}{{\leq}}(4\ell_{W,0,L}r^{K}B)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{W}^{2}W^{2}}+6\frac{B^{2}}{T^{2}}L^{2}\frac{(W-1)W(2W-1)}{6}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#Thmlem1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Optimal 𝛽 for minimizing 𝑔(𝛽,𝐿,𝑟): ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Towards a Golden Classifier-Free Guidance Path via Foresight Fixed Point Iterations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></mtext></mover><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\lx@cref{creftype~refnum}{lem:fixed_point_error}}}{{\leq}}(4\ell_{W,0,L}r^{K}B)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{W}^{2}W^{2}}+6\frac{B^{2}}{T^{2}}L^{2}\frac{(W-1)W(2W-1)}{6}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, summing over all intervals:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E57X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E57X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E57X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E57Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E57Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{M}\sum_{t=1}^{W}\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{iW-W+t},iW-W+t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{iW-W+t},iW-W+t\right)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>W</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{M}\sum_{t=1}^{W}\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{iW-W+t},iW-W+t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{iW-W+t},iW-W+t\right)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E57Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E57Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i=1}^{M}\Bigg((4\ell_{iW,(i-1)W,L}r^{K}B)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i=1}^{M}\Bigg((4\ell_{iW,(i-1)W,L}r^{K}B)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E57Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E57Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+6\frac{B^{2}}{T^{2}}L^{2}\frac{(W-1)W(2W-1)}{6}\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+6\frac{B^{2}}{T^{2}}L^{2}\frac{(W-1)W(2W-1)}{6}\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E57Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E57Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle MW=T}}{{=}}B^{2}\Bigg(16\sum_{i=1}^{T/W}\ell_{iW,(i-1)W,L}^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}r^{2K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mover><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle MW=T}}{{=}}B^{2}\Bigg(16\sum_{i=1}^{T/W}\ell_{iW,(i-1)W,L}^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}r^{2K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E57Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E57Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+6\frac{L^{2}(W-1)(2W-1)}{6T}\Bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+6\frac{L^{2}(W-1)(2W-1)}{6T}\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Expanding <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{iW,(i-1)W,L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{iW,(i-1)W,L}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E58X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E58X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E58X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E58Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E58Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 16B^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{T/W}\left((|\lambda_{iW}|L+|\mu_{iW}|)W+1\right)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}r^{2K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 16B^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{T/W}\left((|\lambda_{iW}|L+|\mu_{iW}|)W+1\right)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}r^{2K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E58Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E58Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+6B^{2}\frac{L^{2}(W-1)(2W-1)}{6T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+6B^{2}\frac{L^{2}(W-1)(2W-1)}{6T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E58Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E58Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(W-1)(2W-1)\leq 2\beta^{2}T^{2}}}{{\leq}}16B^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{T/W}\left((|\lambda_{iW}|L+|\mu_{iW}|)W+1\right)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}r^{2K}+6B^{2}\frac{L^{2}2\beta^{2}T^{2}}{6T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mover><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\stackrel{{\scriptstyle(W-1)(2W-1)\leq 2\beta^{2}T^{2}}}{{\leq}}16B^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{T/W}\left((|\lambda_{iW}|L+|\mu_{iW}|)W+1\right)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}r^{2K}+6B^{2}\frac{L^{2}2\beta^{2}T^{2}}{6T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E58Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E58Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq B^{2}\times 16\sum_{i=1}^{T/W}\left((|\lambda_{iW}|L+|\mu_{iW}|)W+1\right)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}r^{2K}+B^{2}T(2L^{2}\beta^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>16</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>β</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq B^{2}\times 16\sum_{i=1}^{T/W}\left((|\lambda_{iW}|L+|\mu_{iW}|)W+1\right)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}r^{2K}+B^{2}T(2L^{2}\beta^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{iW}|,|\mu_{iW}|,i\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{iW}|,|\mu_{iW}|,i\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math> are constants, and we define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}=16\sum_{i=1}^{T/W}\left((|\lambda_{iW}|L+|\mu_{iW}|)W+1\right)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}/T=\Theta(L^{2})+\Theta(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}=16\sum_{i=1}^{T/W}\left((|\lambda_{iW}|L+|\mu_{iW}|)W+1\right)^{2}\frac{C^{2}(3W-2)}{c^{2}\lambda_{iW}^{2}W^{2}}/T=\Theta(L^{2})+\Theta(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, grouping terms:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E59X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E59X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mi>u</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\left\|\varepsilon^{c}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)-\varepsilon^{u}\left(\hat{x}_{t},t\right)\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E59X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq B^{2}Tg(\beta,L,r)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq B^{2}Tg(\beta,L,r),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\beta,L,r)=\left(\Theta(1)+\Theta(L^{2})\right)r^{2\beta N}+2L^{2}\beta^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\beta,L,r)=\left(\Theta(1)+\Theta(L^{2})\right)r^{2\beta N}+2L^{2}\beta^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we demonstrate the specific setup of the experiment, including the dataset, metrics, and hyperparameter settings for different methods.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Datasets.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The evaluation leverages four datasets to assess text-to-image models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pick-a-Pic</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> collects real-world user preferences from a text-to-image web app. For each prompt, users compare two generated images and select their preferred option (or mark a tie). We use the first 100 prompts from this dataset to test model performance.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DrawBench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> is a comprehensive and challenging benchmark with <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>200 prompts spanning 11 categories like color, counting, and text rendering. These prompts test how well models handle complex or ambiguous descriptions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GenEval</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> evaluates whether generated images correctly follow object-focused instructions. Its 553 prompts cover object placement, quantity, color, leveraging object detection models to evaluate text-to-image models on a variety of generation tasks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PartiPrompts</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> contains 1,600+ diverse prompts covering creative, technical, and abstract concepts. We randomly pick 100 prompts to assess how models balance language understanding and visual creativity.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Metrics. </h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Four metrics are employed to quantify image quality and alignment.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Aesthetic Score (AES)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> quantifies assigning scores (often 1–10) of visual quality by analyzing contrast, composition, color harmony, and detail richness. AES reflects human aesthetic preferences to help refine image generation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ImageReward (IR)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> is a reward model trained on 137,000 expert comparisons using rating/ranking methods, which can be integrated with reinforcement learning to enhance output alignment with human preferences.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Human Preference Score v2 (HPSv2)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> is fine-tuned from CLIP based on Human Preference Dataset v2 with 798,090 human preference choices. HPSv2 can predicts authentic human perceptions of beauty and style.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CLIPScore</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> measures text-image alignment via CLIP embedding cosine similarity. This metric is essential in text-to-image synthesis, ensuring that generated visuals maintain semantic alignment.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T11" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>Performance under different hyperparameter settings. Dataset: Pick-a-Pic; NFE: 100.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T11.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A4.T11.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
